# Denylist build context for the production image (ticket 29).
#
# The DB image has its own copy, db/Dockerfile.dockerignore (ticket 50):
# keep the security entries below (.env*, *.pem, the CA bundle exception)
# the same in both.
#
# `.env*` is the critical entry: `next build` copies `.env` and
# `.env.production` into `.next/standalone`, so a local env file left in the
# context would ship inside the image.
.env*
*.pem
# Ticket 40: the public RDS CA bundle the image verifies RDS TLS against.
!certs/rds-global-bundle.pem

# VCS, dependencies and build output: rebuilt inside the image.
.git
node_modules
.next
dist

# Local tooling, test and log output.
coverage
logs
e2e/.auth
test-results
playwright-report
blob-report
graphify-out
docs/.vitepress/cache
docs/.vitepress/dist
.claude
.venv
*.tsbuildinfo
TODO.md

# Ticket 50: everything the app isn't built from (tickets, docs, infra, CI,
# the DB image, tests and tooling config), so a release that touches only
# these builds the identical image and `publish` pushes nothing. With CI's
# fixed SOURCE_DATE_EPOCH and a warm layer cache, unchanged inputs give an
# unchanged config digest. A file the build needs must not be listed here;
# the build fails if one is.
backlog
docs
infra
db
e2e
.github
**/*.test.ts
**/*.test.tsx
*.md
LICENSE
.gitignore
lefthook.yml
docker-compose.yml
drizzle.config.ts
eslint.config.mjs
playwright.config.ts
tsconfig.playwright.json
vitest.config.ts
trivy-secret.yaml
.trivyignore
